  "outcome": "Shared frontend HTTP/WASM source handling fixes, prompt asynchronous cancellation and recoverable module loading, plus faster Base64 upload preparation. No backend conversion logic added.",
  "changes": [
    "HTTP and WASM adapters download HTTP(S), blob:, root-relative and ./ or ../ paths even when the source name equals its URL; other strings remain inline text.",
    "Binary percent-escaped data URLs preserve their original bytes, literal plus signs and UTF-8 text. Missing data separators reject instead of uploading URL text.",
    "HTTP cancellation is checked before input preparation, headers and POST, and races pending downloads, fetches and response bodies; failed or cancelled source downloads cannot submit conversion requests.",
    "WASM cancellation races Blob reads, source fetches, shared module loading and instantiation, with checks before starting synchronous WASM.",
    "Failed module loads and image ABI initialization can be retried. Concurrent callers reuse shared loading, successful modules stay cached and cancelling one invocation does not cancel another.",
    "HTTP Blob construction snapshots exact typed-array views without a redundant manual copy; SharedArrayBuffer views retain an explicit snapshot. The public WASM runner still snapshots invocation files before awaiting module loading.",
    "A preallocated Base64 byte loop replaces the per-byte Uint8Array.from callback; HTTP and WASM reuse one data URL implementation."
  ],
